 ],
 "notes": "Schedule UTC is the AWS Backup default so no timezone check. Cross-account copy (core) accepts a planned destination ARN with the stated account or a declared copy destination built from a variable/local (planned ARNs are often unknown); the default account ID and default-on toggle are separate detail checks. A single-expression variable reference (not_resources = var.x) is shown resolved to its default in __declared__, so the exclusion list variable is checked via the selection declaring not_resources. 'Configurable secondary region' is checked as a variable whose default is a region name (secondary_region_configurable); the vault/provider is not bound to that variable, since a provider alias or region argument fed by a variable is resolved to its default. cross_region_vault's declared region/provider branches do not compare against the primary vault's region (schema cannot), so a same-region vault with an explicit region argument would pass; kept as Partial. Timezone is not checked: a non-UTC schedule_expression_timezone would pass."
}